`bd-divisions-to-unions`

Installation:

```bash
npm install bd-divisions-to-unions
```

If the project uses pnpm or yarn, use the equivalent installation command.

**THIS PACKAGE IS REQUIRED. DO NOT SUBSTITUTE IT WITH HARDCODED LOCATION DATA OR AN UNRELATED ADDRESS LIBRARY.**

Official package reference:

https://www.npmjs.com/package/bd-divisions-to-unions

Documentation:

https://github.com/Azim-Ahmed/bd-divisons-to-unions

## 2.1 Required Package Functions

Use the package's actual documented functions:

```typescript
import {
  getAllDivision,
  getDistricts,
  getUpazilas,
  getUnions
} from "bd-divisions-to-unions";
```

Use the actual package exports and TypeScript definitions. Do not invent function names or data structures.

Required hierarchy:

```text
Division
   ↓
District
   ↓
Upazila
   ↓
Union
```

Use the package's actual returned values and IDs.

Support Bangla labels by default where appropriate. English labels may be supported through the package's documented language parameter.

Do not manually recreate the package's location dataset.

## 2.2 Cascading Address Dropdowns

Implement a dependent dropdown system.

When the customer selects a Division:

- Load only the Districts belonging to that Division.

When the customer selects a District:

- Load only the Upazilas belonging to that District.

When the customer selects an Upazila:

- Load only the Unions belonging to that Upazila.

When the parent selection changes:

- Clear invalid child selections.
- Reset dependent dropdown values.
- Prevent submitting inconsistent location combinations.

Example:

```text
Division: ঢাকা
District: ঢাকা
Upazila: সাভার
Union: [Actual unions returned by the package]
```

This is an illustrative example. Actual options must come from the package.

## 2.3 Important Geographic Edge Case

Bangladesh city corporations and metropolitan areas may not map neatly to a Union.

Do not force an incorrect Union selection or fabricate an administrative location for an urban address.

Use the mandatory package for the supported administrative hierarchy. Where the selected location has no applicable Union, provide an appropriate area, ward, or locality field and handle it explicitly.

Keep this exception compatible with the same address and order data model.

## 2.4 Package Integration Requirements

- Install the exact required dependency.
- Inspect the package version and exports.
- Verify frontend bundler compatibility.
- Verify backend runtime compatibility.
- Handle CommonJS/ESM interoperability correctly.
- Reuse the package rather than copying its dataset.
- Avoid duplicate location datasets.
- Ensure the selected parent-child hierarchy is valid.
